course: dictionary
lesson: 15558
title: Supplementation: adding what is missing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Supplementation is a noun. It means adding something extra to make something complete, or to make up for what is missing. The ending -ation often turns an action into a name, so supplementation is the act of supplementing.
explain: Most often it is about food and health. «In winter, Ruby's doctor said she needed vitamin D supplementation, because she gets very little sunshine.» Her body is short of vitamin D, so she takes extra to make up for it.
explain: Read the clues around the word. The words «extra» and «make up for what is missing» tell you the meaning. Then swap in your meaning, "adding something extra", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word also works in school and money. «The school got extra funding as supplementation, so it could hire another teacher.» Doctors decide on supplementation, because too much of some vitamins can harm you.
fact: Supplementation means adding something extra to make something complete or to make up for what is missing.
fact: «Supplementation» is an uncountable noun: you say some supplementation, not "a supplementation".
fact: Vitamin D supplementation is often advised in winter in the UK, Ireland and Canada, when there is little sunshine.
fact: Iron supplementation may be needed by some people.
fact: Doctors decide on supplementation, because too much of some vitamins can harm you.
exercise: «Winter has little sunshine, so the doctor advised vitamin D supplementation.» What does supplementation mean here? | Taking away something harmful | Playing sports in the sun | *Adding something extra to make up for what is missing | Losing weight quickly
exercise: Ella thinks supplementation is a verb, like run. What is the right answer? | It is a verb, so you say they supplementation every day | *It is a noun, so you can say some supplementation | It is an adjective, like happy | It is a place where people go to swim
exercise: Which of these is an example of supplementation? | Painting a picture of the sea | Running fast on a cold winter morning | Reading a book quietly in bed | *Taking iron tablets because a doctor says your iron is low
test: «The school got extra money as supplementation, so it could hire another teacher.» What is the best meaning of supplementation here? | *Extra money added to make up for what was missing | A new school building | Money taken away from the school | A holiday for the teachers
test: Mia says, «Vitamin D supplementation is always safe, so I can take as much as I like.» What is the mistake? | *Too much of some vitamins can harm you | Vitamin D is a fruit | Winter has lots of sunshine | Doctors never give advice on vitamins
exam: Which sentence uses supplementation correctly? | The children supplementation ran to school | Supplementation swam across the lake | Supplementation is a sunny day in the park | *The doctor advised iron supplementation because Sam was short of iron
